---Details about the branch continuous backup configuration
---@class xata.BackupConfiguration
---@field retentionPeriod? number Number of days of point-in-time recovery to guarantee. You can restore the branch to any point within this many days. To provide this, the most recent full backup taken before the start of the window is always kept, along with all changes made after it. Because of this, restore points older than retentionPeriod are sometimes available, but how far back they go depends on the backup schedule and is not guaranteed.
---@field backupTime? string When to take a full backup, in UTC, in the format D:HH:MM. D is * for every day, or 0-6 for one day of the week (0 is Sunday). If it is not set, a random time on Sunday between 02:00 and 05:59 is used.

